      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "633612beac98d218a27f674b",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Agreed. It is ridiculous how much there is and how negatively it affects video recordings as well.\n\nI understand it's necessary to reduce artifacts on the DoF shader, but it would be great if we could toggle it. It could be like the Near Clip feature, where it could reset when the user closes the camera.\n\nHere's a visual comparison of No AF vs S-AF. It's ridiculous. It's worse than my Nikon D3200 on high ISO in the dark.",
