  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-29T21:48:46.448Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I would like to see a toggle to the noise added on the in game camera when depth of field is activated.\nI understand the noise is to be used as a sort of dithering to break up banding and help with compression artifacts. But I record using lossless and I usually add my own film grain in post to do that. \nIt just degrades the quality of videos and requires unnecessary denoising in my video editing software (which takes a lot of render time, denoising is not an easy task in Davinci Resolve to render)",
